sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    participant Client as MCP Client<br/>(Claude, Cursor, etc.)
    participant Proxy as MCP Auth Adapter
    participant SSO as Upstream IdP
    participant MCPServer as MCP Server

    Note over Client, MCPServer: 1. Discovery
    Client->>MCPServer: Connects to server
    MCPServer-->>Client: Announces MCP Auth Adapter as Authorization Server
    Client->>Proxy: GET /.well-known/openid-configuration
    Proxy->>SSO: GET /.well-known/openid-configuration
    SSO-->>Proxy: Returns descriptor
    Proxy-->>Client: Returns filtered descriptor (issuer=adapter_issuer, iss_supported=true,<br/>authorization/token endpoints=adapter, scopes adapted)

    Note over Client, SSO: 2. Open Dynamic Client Registration (DCR)
    Client->>Proxy: POST /register
    Proxy-->>Client: Returns pre-configured fixed client_id from Upstream IdP

    Note over Client, SSO: 3. Authorization with RFC 9207 iss verification
    Client->>Proxy: GET /authorize (client_id, redirect_uri=client_callback, state=client_state, scopes)
    Note over Proxy: Validates redirect_uri against allowed patterns<br/>Filters scopes (e.g. strips "offline_access")<br/>Signs state blob: HMAC({redirect_uri, state, exp}, secret)
    Proxy-->>Client: 302 → Upstream IdP /authorize<br/>(redirect_uri=adapter/callback, state=signed_blob, filtered scopes)
    Client->>SSO: GET /authorize (client_id, redirect_uri=adapter/callback, state=signed_blob)
    Note over SSO: Authenticates user, consent screen shown
    SSO-->>Client: 302 → adapter/callback?code=X&state=signed_blob&iss=upstream_issuer
        
    Client->>Proxy: GET /authorize/callback?code=X&state=signed_blob&iss=upstream_issuer
    Note over Proxy: Verifies state HMAC signature & expiration<br/>Validates upstream iss parameter<br/>Extracts original redirect_uri and state
    Proxy-->>Client: 302 → client_callback?code=X&state=client_state&iss=adapter_issuer
    Note over Client: Validates iss to be adapter_issuer<br/>from the discovered descriptor

    Note over Client, SSO: 4. Token Exchange (via Adapter Proxy)
    Client->>Proxy: POST /token (code=X, redirect_uri=client_callback)
    Note over Proxy: Validates redirect_uri, rewrites to adapter/callback
    Proxy->>SSO: POST /token (code=X, redirect_uri=adapter/callback)
    Note over SSO: Validates redirect_uri to be the same as during Authorization
    SSO-->>Proxy: Returns Access and Refresh Token
    Proxy-->>Client: Forwards Access and Refresh Token

    Note over Client, MCPServer: 5. Secure Resource Access & Access Token Validation
    Client->>MCPServer: Sends MCP request (e.g. tool call) with Access Token
    MCPServer->>Proxy: GET /.well-known/openid-configuration
    Proxy-->>MCPServer: Returns descriptor containing JWKS (Certificate) URI from Upstream IdP
    MCPServer-->>SSO: Fetches Certificate used to sign Access Token
    MCPServer->>MCPServer: Validates the Access Token signature & claims<br/>Authenticates and authorizes request
